  annotation (Documentation(info = "<html><body><p>Mirvetuximab soravtansine is an antibody-drug conjugate used to treat ovarian, fallopian tube, and peritoneal cancers. It is authorised in the European Union and is also being investigated for other uses.</p><p><small>Summary written by glm-5.3-flash from <a href=\"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q115285803\">Wikidata Q115285803</a> and the WHO ATC classification and the EMA medicines list; not checked by a person.</small></p><table><tr><td>name:</td><td>mirvetuximab soravtansine</td></tr><tr><td>ATC codes:</td><td>L01FX26</td></tr><tr><td>DrugBank:</td><td><a href=\"https://go.drugbank.com/drugs/DB12489\">DB12489</a></td></tr><tr><td>PubChem CID:</td><td><a href=\"https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/131704323\">131704323</a></td></tr><tr><td>Wikidata:</td><td><a href=\"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q115285803\">Q115285803</a></td></tr><tr><td>molar mass:</td><td>150000 g/mol (Drugs.Common 25.09, not verified)</td></tr></table></body></html>"));
